course: dictionary
lesson: 4699
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Honey» can be a sweet food, or a loving name for someone. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because the clues in the sentence show which meaning fits.
explain: Look at «Put honey on your toast» and then at «Thanks, honey, that was lovely.» In the first, honey is the golden food. In the second, someone is using it as a name for a person they love. Ask yourself: does this meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Words also appear in phrases. «As sweet as honey» means kind and gentle. A honeybee is a bee that makes honey, and a honeycomb is the wax home where bees store it. Once you know one meaning, the others can often be worked out from the context.
fact: Honey is a sweet, thick, golden food made by bees from the nectar of flowers.
fact: «Honey» can also be a loving name for someone, like «dear» or «sweetie».
fact: Bees store honey in a honeycomb and need it for food in winter.
fact: «Winnie the Pooh only wants the honey»: in stories, bears love honey, but a real bear raiding a bee nest also eats the grubs.
fact: Honey is measured in jars, kilograms or spoons.
exercise: «Put a spoon of honey in your tea.» What is honey in this sentence? | A kind of bread | A small insect with a sting | A loving name for someone | *A sweet, thick, golden food made by bees
exercise: «Thanks, honey, that was lovely.» What does honey mean in this sentence? | A bee's home | *A loving name for someone | A sweet, golden drink | Sticky food for winter
exercise: Why do bees need honey? | *To have food in winter | To make the flowers grow | To paint pictures | To make bread
test: What is a honeybee? | A flower full of nectar | A honey-coloured stone | *A bee that makes honey | A bear that eats honey
test: «The stone was honey-coloured, like the old buildings in Bath.» What does honey-coloured mean? | *Golden, like honey | Sticky and wet | Black as coal | Sweet to taste
exam: Jayden reads «Honey, pass the honey.» What does the second honey mean? | A loving name for someone | Kind | A kind of bear | *The sweet, golden food
